---
/**
 * 证书页。数字全部来自 原始资料/ 与 证书/ 里的原件：
 *   ISO 9001  Reg 0350525Q30204R1S  2025-07-07 → 2028-07-06
 *   ISO 14001 Reg 0350525E20142R1S  2025-07-07 → 2028-07-06
 *   ISO 45001 Reg 0350525S30123R1S  2025-07-07 → 2028-07-06
 *   中国环境标志 CEC2025ELP00927817（直接接触皮肤）
 *                CEC2025ELP00927818（非直接接触皮肤）
 *                2025-05-12 → 2028-05-11
 * 以上持有人是 青岛千惠绣品有限公司（Qianhui Embroidery），不是集团名。
 *
 * 测试报告都是开给供应商/工厂的，不是开给千惠的，页面必须写明：
 *   16 CFR 1633  SGS Shunde  SDFTS25002706R05_EN  2025-07-24  持证人 Foshan Shunde Weishini
 *                样品 RAZ-US，99×191×25 cm，无床架；3 件全过
 *   16 CFR 1633  STC Guangdong  DT26061734  2026-07-01  申请人 Dongguan Haichuan Nonwoven
 *                样品为绗缝（tuft）床垫，Style 008，无床架；构造字段全空
 *   OEKO-TEX 100 SH015 258259  TESTEX  2026-03-03 → 2027-03-31  Class I
 *                持证人 Zhejiang Kaijie，3D 网眼布
 *   RoHS 2.0     STC Guangdong  DT26050904  2026-05-19  江门衡高 海绵
 * 任何一条都不能改写成“千惠持有该证书”。
 */
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { pageTitle } from '@/lib/seo';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '@/lib/schema';

const management = [
  {
    standard: 'ISO 9001:2015 · GB/T 19001-2016',
    name: 'Quality management system',
    reg: '0350525Q30204R1S',
    issued: '7 Jul 2025',
    expires: '6 Jul 2028',
  },
  {
    standard: 'ISO 14001:2015 · GB/T 24001-2016',
    name: 'Environmental management system',
    reg: '0350525E20142R1S',
    issued: '7 Jul 2025',
    expires: '6 Jul 2028',
  },
  {
    standard: 'ISO 45001:2018 · GB/T 45001-2020',
    name: 'Occupational health and safety',
    reg: '0350525S30123R1S',
    issued: '7 Jul 2025',
    expires: '6 Jul 2028',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle('Certifications & Test Reports')}
  description="ISO 9001, ISO 14001, ISO 45001 and China Environmental Label certificate numbers and expiry dates, plus the 16 CFR 1633, OEKO-TEX and RoHS reports on file, with laboratory and holder named."
  jsonld={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Certifications', path: '/certifications/' }])]}
>
  <div class="container-page py-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Certifications' }]} />
  </div>

  <section class="container-page pb-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Certifications &amp; test reports</h1>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
      <p>
        The management-system certificates and the China Environmental Label are held by
        Qingdao Qianhui Embroidery Co., Ltd., the group company that manufactures bedding at the
        Jimo site. Each entry gives the registration number and expiry date, so a vendor file can
        be checked against the original rather than against a logo on a website.
      </p>
      <p>
        The test reports further down the page were issued to the factories and material
        suppliers we buy from, not to Qianhui. That distinction matters when your file is audited,
        so we state it on each one. None of the management-system certificates is a product test.
        For a US mattress the document that matters is a 16 CFR 1633 report, and those are listed
        with their report numbers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-page py-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Management system certificates</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[40rem] border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-line text-left text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-600">
            <th scope="col" class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Standard</th>
            <th scope="col" class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Registration no.</th>
            <th scope="col" class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Issued</th>
            <th scope="col" class="py-3 font-semibold">Expires</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            management.map((row) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                <td class="py-3 pr-4">
                  <p class="font-medium text-ink-900">{row.standard}</p>
                  <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-ink-600">{row.name}</p>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-xs text-ink-600">{row.reg}</td>
                <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-ink-600">{row.issued}</td>
                <td class="py-3 text-ink-600">{row.expires}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
      <p>
        Issued by Xingyuan Certification Centre Co., Ltd. (Beijing), accredited by CNAS under
        C035-M and a member of the IAF multilateral recognition arrangement. The scope on each
        certificate reads: products and production of beddings, woven garments (cotton
        overcoats, thermal jackets, cotton wear) and tents, at No. 208 Yanqing First-Class Road,
        Jimo District, Qingdao.
      </p>
      <p>
        A management system certificate covers how the plant runs. It does not certify the
        performance of a particular sheet or towel. For that, see the product test section
        below.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-page py-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">China Environmental Label</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
      Two certificates under HJ 2546-2016, the textile product standard of the China
      Environmental Label programme. Both were issued on 12 May 2025 and run to 11 May 2028.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">Direct contact with skin</p>
        <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-ink-600">CEC2025ELP00927817</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600">
          Covers the bed sheets, duvet covers, pillowcases, face and hand towels, bath towels,
          bath mats, quilts and blankets listed in the certificate annex, in cotton and
          polyester constructions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900">Not in direct contact with skin</p>
        <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-ink-600">CEC2025ELP00927818</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600">
          Covers the products listed in its own annex. Ask us for the annex if your order falls
          under this category and you need the item list.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
      Issued by China Environmental United Certification Center (CEC) under authorisation from
      the Ministry of Ecology and Environment. The annex does not list bathrobes, slippers or
      mattresses, so do not read this label as covering those lines. If your order includes
      them, ask what documentation applies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container-page py-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Test reports on file</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
      Four reports. Each is current at the time of writing, and each PDF names the plant it was
      issued to. Ask for the PDF with your quote rather than taking a number from this page. We
      keep the supplier names out of the page copy, not out of the documents.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-6">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">16 CFR 1633, pocket-spring mattress</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-ink-600">SDFTS25002706R05_EN · SGS Shunde · 24 Jul 2025</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          The US open-flame standard. SGS tested a pocket innerspring and foam mattress with a
          flame-retardant cotton barrier, flame-retardant cloth ticking and no foundation. The
          sample was 99 × 191 × 25 cm. Three specimens peaked at 31.7, 31.3 and 31.3 kW against
          a 200 kW limit, and released 2.0, 2.0 and 1.9 MJ in the first ten minutes against a
          15 MJ limit. All three passed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          The laboratory holds CPSC identification number 1621. The report was issued to a
          mattress factory in Foshan, not to Qianhui. It covers one prototype at one size. The
          sets we sell are produced in China to that build, and with every US order we send a
          signed statement from the factory that the order follows the tested prototype. That
          statement, not the report on its own, is what ties a shipment to the test.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          Read it as a prototype test, not a shipment certificate. Its origin and supplier
          fields describe the sample that was tested. They do not describe the sets in your
          order.
        </p>
        <a href="/guides/16-cfr-1633-hotel-mattress/" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm font-semibold underline">
          What 16 CFR 1633 requires
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">16 CFR 1633, barrier supplier report</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-ink-600">DT26061734 · STC Guangdong · 1 Jul 2026</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          A second open-flame report, this one from the nonwoven barrier supplier. Three tufted
          mattress sets, style 008, no foundation. Peak heat release was 31.5, 31.2 and 31.7 kW;
          first ten minutes 2.2, 2.1 and 2.2 MJ. All passed. The laboratory is CNAS accredited
          under L3428.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          The construction fields on this report are blank, so we treat it as evidence for the
          barrier, not as the compliance report for a mattress you order. It is the other
          document we send if your buyer asks what the barrier has been tested with.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">OEKO-TEX STANDARD 100, 3D mesh fabric</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-ink-600">SH015 258259 · TESTEX · 3 Mar 2026 to 31 Mar 2027</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          Product class I, the baby-article class, for tri-dimensional knitted 3D mesh fabric in
          white polyester, Lyocell or viscose, with polyester interlining and backing. The holder
          is the fabric mill. Class I is the strictest of the four classes.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          The certificate covers the fabric. It does not cover a finished mattress, sheet or
          towel, and we do not describe our own products as OEKO-TEX certified on the strength of
          it. If your spec names OEKO-TEX, tell us which component needs to be covered.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">RoHS 2.0, polyurethane sponge</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-ink-600">DT26050904 · STC Guangdong · 19 May 2026</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          One sponge sample tested against EU Directive 2011/65/EU and (EU) 2015/863. It passed.
          The applicant is the foam supplier. Ask for the PDF if you need the name.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          RoHS restricts substances in electrical and electronic equipment. It says nothing about
          flammability or skin contact, so we do not present it as a textile certification. It is
          listed here because buyers sometimes ask for it by name.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">16 CFR 1632, mattresses and pads</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          The cigarette-ignition standard is a separate test with a separate report. It applies
          to mattresses and to mattress pads, which means a 1633 report does not cover the
          protectors on the same order.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          There is no 1632 report among the documents above. If your order includes protectors
          and the spec names 1632, say so at inquiry stage so the test can be arranged before
          production rather than after the goods are packed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Records for a US import</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          Under 16 CFR 1633 the manufacturer and the importer each keep the test report, the
          prototype description and a certification on file. On an FOB or CIF shipment the
          importer of record is normally the buyer or the buyer's customs broker. We are not the
          US importer of record and we do not act as one.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          We supply what the importer needs to keep: the report, the prototype description and
          the factory statement that the order matches it. If your compliance team wants a
          different form of wording, send their template and we will ask the factory to sign it
          before production.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Things we do not claim</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          We hold no OEKO-TEX, GOTS, BS 7177 or EN 597 certificate for the finished sheets, towels
          or mattresses. The OEKO-TEX certificate above belongs to a fabric mill and covers one
          3D mesh fabric. If your spec sheet names a standard we do not hold, say so at inquiry
          stage. We will either quote the testing properly or tell you we cannot meet it, before
          a container is booked rather than after.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          BS 7177 and EN 597 are the UK and European counterparts to the US rules, and they test
          differently. A US report says nothing about either.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">How to check a certificate</h2>
        <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          <li>
            The holder's name. Our management-system certificates are held by Qianhui Embroidery,
            not by the group trade name, and the test reports were issued to the manufacturers.
            Make sure the name matches the entity on your invoice, and know which company a
            report was actually issued to.
          </li>
          <li>The registration number and expiry date, checked against the issuing body.</li>
          <li>
            The scope or annex, checked against what you are buying. A certificate for bed linen
            does not cover slippers, and a report for a sponge does not cover a mattress.
          </li>
          <li>
            For product tests, the laboratory's accreditation, the build described and the size
            tested. See the four checks in the 16 CFR 1633 guide.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-page py-10">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Ask for the originals with the quote</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600">
        Tell us the destination country and the standard on your spec sheet. We will send the
        certificates and reports that apply, and say plainly which ones we do not have.
      </p>
      <a href="/request-a-quote/" class="mt-4 inline-block rounded-md bg-brand-600 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white">
        Request a quote
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
